The workflow is built, saved to slot main-rB and starts correctly. I sent one test message and it replied with the right opening: "Hello, this is the digital assistant calling from Freya Bank; this call is recorded. Am I speaking with Ms Lee?" I did not run any practice cases, and that one message is the only live test.

**How the call flows:** the date code you supplied runs first, then opening, identity check, account lookup, the main collection conversation, and the end of the call.
- **Opening:** handles who answers, including a relative, callback, wrong number, deceased and unclear cases.
- **Identity check:** asks the two security questions in turn.
- **Account lookup:** runs on its own and uses your account hook code exactly as given.
- **Main conversation:** handles Brief B's rules: every product is stated first, then one "pay all today?" question, then each product in turn with its own attempt count. All promises are read back once with one "Do you confirm?", then recorded one per product. Products without a promise get a note, and there are no notes when a transfer happens.
- **Close codes:** the close step follows the outcome rules from both briefs.

**Rule choices:**
- **Failed recordings:** a failed `create_promise` is tried once more. A second failure marks that product `service_error`, and the call carries on with the others, as the Brief B memo says.
- **Deadlines:** the memos' 12 and 7 business days match the date facts, so nothing differs from the brief.

The structure check and the wording gate both show 0 errors. I did not get to the final rule-by-rule re-read against the brief before time ran short.

